<surname>Leto</surname><given-names>K.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>McIntosh</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nuclear mutation leads to an accelerated turnover of chloroplast-encoded 48 kD and 34.5 kD polypeptides in thylakoids lacking photosystem II</article-title><source>EMBO (Eur. Mol. Biol. Organ.) J.</source><volume>4</volume><year>1985</year><fpage>1645</fpage><lpage>1653</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Lietal1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>X.</given-names></name><name><surname>Henry</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Yuan</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cline</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffman</surname><given-names>N.E.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A chloroplast homologue of the signal recognition particle subunit SRP54 is involved in the posttranslational integration of a protein into thylakoid membranes</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source><volume>92</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>3789</fpage><lpage>3793</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7731984</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Matlacketal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Matlack</surname><given-names>K.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mothes</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rapoport</surname><given-names>T.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Protein translocationtunnel vision</article-title><source>Cell.</source><volume>92</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>381</fpage><lpage>390</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9476897</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="McCartyetal1991"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCarty</sur